findings.body:
**The floor takes the first call in the window, not the transcript's first request.** ADR 0122 defines the floor as "the median of each transcript's first request". But `scanLine` drops every entry before `sinceMs` (`if (Number.isNaN(at) || at < sinceMs) return;`, L265) before any call is recorded. `addCalls` then takes the floor from `index === 0` of the calls that are left:

```ts
const ordered = [...calls].sort((a, b) => a.at - b.at);
for (const [index, call] of ordered.entries()) {
  ...
  if (index === 0) bucket.floors.push(contextOf(call));
  const again = recachedTokens(call, ordered[index - 1]);
```

No mtime or start-time check keeps a transcript that spans the window edge out of the report.

**Failing input.** Take a conductor or console transcript that started 8 days ago and is still in use. With the default 7-day window, its first in-window call might have 150k context, and that value becomes its "first-request floor". The conductor row often has only one or a few transcripts, so its floor is mostly that mid-session number. `noteOrigin` already runs before the filter ("whatever the window") so that classing uses the real start. The floor needs the same care.

**The same cause hides re-caches.** The first in-window call has no `previous`, so an idle gap of more than an hour across the window edge is never counted as a re-cache.

**Fix.** Track whether the transcript's real first assistant call falls inside the window, and push a floor only in that case. Seed `previous` with the last call before the window.

https://github.com/AlexisBalayre/pupitre/blob/7e7f202f040cca91e4f68fa1a08e89e6a8ac964a/src/core/usage-report.service.ts#L395-L407

findings.suggestion:
function textOf(content: unknown): string {
  if (typeof content === 'string') return content;
  return blocksOf(content)
    .map((block) => {
      if (typeof block.content === 'string') return block.content;
      const text = (block as { text?: unknown }).text;
      return typeof text === 'string' ? text : '';
    })
    .join('');
}
